test(server): remove ambient-brief flake from full-suite run (v0.5.4)

server.test.ts could intermittently fail in afterAll with
addedDocuments containing jarvis-brief-ambient-*.md files. These
files come from the ambient action subscriber's 60s setInterval,
which always registered even when HARNESS_AMBIENT_ENABLED was unset
(the daemon gate only short-circuited inside the timer callback).
Under the full Jest run the timer had time to fire and the diff
caught the resulting writes. The test passed in isolation.

- src/web/server.ts: gate the action-subscriber setInterval on
  HARNESS_AMBIENT_ENABLED === '1', matching the daemon's own gate
  above it. Non-ambient runs no longer register the timer at all,
  eliminating the race window.
- src/testSupport/harnessCleanup.test-support.ts: defensive filter
  on jarvis-brief-ambient-* in listHarnessDocumentFiles so the
  snapshot/diff cannot flake even if a developer environment does
  enable ambient mode. The diff is for policing test API mutations,
  not independent timer work.
- src/testSupport/harnessCleanup.test-support.test.ts: 1 new test
  pinning the filter contract — ambient briefs are excluded but a
  genuine test-leaked document still surfaces in addedDocuments.

Full suite 1740 -> 1741 tests. No behaviour change when
HARNESS_AMBIENT_ENABLED=1.

